or the vector field $G,$ we have $P={2}^{2x+y+1}$ and $Q={2}^{2x+y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={2}^{2x+y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={2}^{2x+y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)$ and $Q=\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{{y}^{2}+1}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{4xy}{{y}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4xy}{{y}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $H$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $G={2}^{2x+y+1}\\,i+{2}^{2x+y}\\,j$; $H=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)\\,i+\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,j$ only." 13194139537063 17592186576411 true] [17592186240912 1071 "Which of the numbers below belong to ${Q}^{-}?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." 13194139537063 17592186576411 true] [17592186240912 1071 "Which of the numbers below belong to ${Q}^{-}?$\n- **I.** $47$\n- **II.** $-\\sqrt{12}$\n- **III.** $\\sqrt{10}$\n- **IV.** $0$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." 13194139537063 17592186576411 false] [17592186240914 1071 "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${R}_{0}^{-}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537063 17592186576411 true] [17592186240914 1071 "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${R}_{0}^{-}?$\n- **I.** $-14$\n- **II.** $\\sqrt{19}$\n- **III.** $-\\frac{2}{7}$\n- **IV.** $0$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537063 17592186576411 false] [17592186240914 1074 "Remember that ${R}_{0}^{-}$ is the set of all negative real numbers and $0.$\n\n- $-14$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $\\sqrt{19}$ is a positive number, so it does *not* belong to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\frac{2}{7}$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{-}.\\,