at has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{L}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}^{U}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ only." 13194139537063 17592186576411 true] [17592186243947 1071 "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537063 17592186576411 true] [17592186243947 1071 "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537063 17592186576411 false] [17592186243947 1074 "Remember that in the LU factor