erval $(-3,0)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d2/d2ed3670f7c67d60c7739ee35d66943b8341b2a49faa97546242609dd39afabc.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139537063 17592186576411 false] [17592186244151 1074 "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-2,0]$ and $x\\in (0,2).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/46/46e1daf2cb9025b6a736f223fbe168ea32b66302cebea23ca3a2d473e78b77b3.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $(-3,0)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d2/d2ed3670f7c67d60c7739ee35d66943b8341b2a49faa97546242609dd39afabc.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in (-2,0]$; $x\\in (0,2)$ only." 13194139537063 17592186576411 true] [17592186244191 1071 "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537063 17592186576411 true] [17592186244191 1071 "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n- **I.** ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}\\,y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}$\n- **II.** ${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}$ $$\n- **III.** ${y}^{′}-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x={y}^{6}$\n\nSelect all that apply." 13194139537063 17592186576411 false] [17592186244191 1074 "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}\\,y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}$ is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\sqrt{x},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=-1.\n$$\n\n- Equation ${